      "content": "Okay, so the research is mixed. But if you look at the biggest players in the S&P 500, most of them have massive DEI departments and are very vocal about it. Doesn't that suggest there's a clear business imperative that's just not fully captured in the academic studies yet? Like, is it basically a proven competitive advantage even if the direct metrics are hard to pin down?",
